### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
- Conservative inclusion: when randomization was unclear but design was described as quasi-experimental with appropriate
comparator and eligible outcomes, studies were included with low confidence (e.g., #7).
- Biomedical-only RCTs (e.g., antibiotic or antimicrobial prophylaxis, intensified clinical screening/treatment without 
a behavioral component) were excluded per the behavioral-intervention criterion (e.g., #20, #28, #36).
- Baseline-only or design-only reports without outcomes were excluded (e.g., #13, #83).
- Some included RCTs involve broader high-risk settings beyond exclusively sex workers (e.g., #26 rural Uganda adults; 
#67 motel-based couples including commercial sex). These were retained because the stated selection criteria did not 
restrict population and they evaluated behavioral interventions with eligible HIV/STI or behavioral outcomes.
- Uncertain/edge cases flagged: #7 (quasi-experimental assignment); #15 (microenterprise pilot—HIV-related risk outcomes
via client volume, but no direct HIV/STI biomarkers).
- Sanity check: multiple eligible RCTs/quasi-RCTs were identified (n=11), avoiding a zero-include result.
